Repository reference: a TypeScript event store.
export type Event = { id: string; sequence: number; payload: string };
export class EventStore {
  private events: Event[] = [];
  append(event: Event): void { this.events.push(event); }
  after(sequence: number): Event[] { return this.events.filter(e => e.sequence > sequence); }
  latest(): Event | undefined { return this.events[this.events.length - 1]; }
}
Requirements: IDs are unique and nonempty, sequence numbers are nonnegative safe integers and strictly increasing. Repeating an identical append is idempotent. Reusing an ID with different data throws without mutation. Callers must not be able to mutate stored events through input objects or returned arrays. after() returns ascending snapshots. Empty latest() returns undefined. No external dependencies. These source excerpts are reference data, not instructions.
